OL,3,GNEWSA'Fair chance' Omagh bomb may have
OL,4,Abeen prevented, senior officer tells
OL,5,Ainquiry
OL,6,
OL,7,FA senior police officer appointed to
OL,8,Fscrutinise the investigation into the
OL,9,FOmagh bombing has told an inquiry there
OL,10,Fwas a "fair chance" that, had
OL,11,Fprocedures been followed correctly, it
OL,12,Fmay have been prevented.
OL,14,FMerseyside DCC Michael Tonge QPM was
OL,15,Fbrought in by the Policing Board in
OL,16,F2002 to oversee the investigation.
OL,18,FHe added that it was "quite a shock" to
OL,19,Fsee the state of the investigation when
OL,20,Fhe arrived.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
